Value chassis_id (.*)
Value system_name (.*)
Value system_description (.*)
Value system_caps_supported (.*)
Value system_caps_enabled (.*)
Value mgmt_type (.*)
Value mgmt_address (.*)

# Parse the output of "show lldp local" on an HP AOS-S switch.
#
# A single logical record: the "LLDP Local Device Information" block. The
# "LLDP Port Information" table that follows is a per-port listing and is
# intentionally ignored - its rules are anchored to the specific label
# lines above so nothing in the table matches.
#
# Notes on the label lines:
#   - "System Capabilities Supported:" and "Enabled:" have no space before
#     the colon, so the rules use \s*: (zero or more).
#   - "Type:" and "Address:" are indented five spaces under the
#     "Management Address :" line; \s+Type does not match
#     "Chassis Type :" because the label word is not the first token.
#   - "Chassis Type : mac-address" is not captured on purpose.


Start
  ^\s+Chassis Id\s*:\s*(?P<chassis_id>\S.*?)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+System Name\s*:\s*(?P<system_name>\S+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+System Description\s*:\s*(?P<system_description>\S.*?)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+System Capabilities Supported\s*:\s*(?P<system_caps_supported>\S+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+System Capabilities Enabled\s*:\s*(?P<system_caps_enabled>\S+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+Type\s*:\s*(?P<mgmt_type>\S+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+Address\s*:\s*(?P<mgmt_address>\S+)\s*$ -> Record
